  "id": "Wandsworth-2025_1760",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development, by reason of its location within an existing residential garden, nor being an established brownfield site while existing within its own established curtilage, would not be an appropriate form of development where national, regional and local planning policies makes presumption against such development due to the harm to the local spatial character that would occur, as in this case. The proposal therefore fails to comply with the policy LP7 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, by reason of its siting, size, scale, form and appearance, the proposal would harm the spatial character, appearance and local distinctiveness afforded by the site to the local area, including the open rear garden setting of the adjoining streetscape while harmfully diminishing the characterful streetscape gap. The development would therefore fail to comply with policy LP1 and LP7 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Housing SPD (2016).",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development, by reason of its scale, design and siting constitutes an unneighbourly form of development that harms the amenity of the neighbouring property in the form of loss outlook and being overbearing. The application has also failed to demonstrate that there would not be unacceptable harm to neighbouring windows in respect to reductions in daylight/sunlight. The development is therefore contrary to policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Housing SPD (2016).",
    "Reason : 4 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan consisting of the Core Strategy, Development Management Policies Document, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
